  "description": "Original study: Berg, J., Dickhaut, J., & McCabe, K. (1995). Trust, reciprocity, and social history. Games and Economic Behavior, 10(1), 122-142. Both people in an anonymous pair received $10. The sender could send any part of it to the receiver; the amount sent was tripled, and the receiver decided how much to send back. Trust games appear in 47 of the 500 studies in our survey. This template follows the no-history condition: one sender, one receiver, $10 each, amount sent tripled, one round. Participants are simulated: each is a Model participant, using the free test model until you choose a model, so the first runs only check the design; with the test model every participant takes the sample answer.",
